From d1cd4203e39c63d0314523ff77b7105d2b0465db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t95 <t95@local>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 21:59:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] hrtimers: reset per-CPU state in hrtimers_prepare_cpu() (T95,
 ACK android12-5.4)

ACK android12-5.4 reverted upstream 5c0930ccaad5 ("hrtimers: Push pending
hrtimers away from outgoing CPU earlier") for ABI reasons, so there is no
CPUHP_AP_HRTIMERS_DYING step. 5.4.290 then picked up 2f8dea1692ee
("hrtimers: Handle CPU state correctly on hotplug"), which moves the reset of
the per-CPU hrtimer state from hrtimers_prepare_cpu() into a new
hrtimers_cpu_starting() callback registered on CPUHP_AP_HRTIMERS_DYING. Without
that step the callback never runs on hotplug, so a CPU that comes back after
suspend (disable_nonboot_cpus) keeps stale hres_active/next_timer/expires_next
and the system hard-locks seconds after resume.

Restore the reset in hrtimers_prepare_cpu(), as before 2f8dea1692ee.
Found by bisect on an Allwinner H616 box: 5.4.288 good, 5.4.290 bad.
---
 kernel/time/hrtimer.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/time/hrtimer.c b/kernel/time/hrtimer.c
index c49c09b60..0d3838cc7 100644
--- a/kernel/time/hrtimer.c
+++ b/kernel/time/hrtimer.c
@@ -2066,6 +2066,20 @@ int hrtimers_prepare_cpu(unsigned int cpu)
 	}
 
 	cpu_base->cpu = cpu;
+	/*
+	 * T95: в ACK android12-5.4 откатили "hrtimers: Push pending hrtimers away from
+	 * outgoing CPU earlier" (нет состояния CPUHP_AP_HRTIMERS_DYING), поэтому
+	 * hrtimers_cpu_starting() при hotplug не вызывается. Состояние per-CPU сбрасываем
+	 * здесь, как до 2f8dea1692ee, иначе после сна (вторичные CPU выключаются и
+	 * включаются) остаются старые hres_active/next_timer -> система зависает.
+	 */
+	cpu_base->active_bases = 0;
+	cpu_base->hres_active = 0;
+	cpu_base->hang_detected = 0;
+	cpu_base->next_timer = NULL;
+	cpu_base->softirq_next_timer = NULL;
+	cpu_base->expires_next = KTIME_MAX;
+	cpu_base->softirq_expires_next = KTIME_MAX;
 	hrtimer_cpu_base_init_expiry_lock(cpu_base);
 	return 0;
 }
